/E (        Student teams need to know what to deliver, when it is due, which work the team actually submitted and which supervisor feedback belongs to that work. Supervisors need to follow only their assigned teams. Informal links and messages make deadlines, version history and private feedback difficult to verify.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
358 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 270 0 R
/E (fastTrack provides one course-project context with explicit Student and Supervisor roles. A team follows a chronological milestone track; students submit work links and supervisors comment on the exact saved submission. The system records identity, version and acceptance time on the server. The course title shown in a future assessed deployment remains a presentation/configuration decision; a multi-course administration system is outside this baseline.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
359 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 270 0 R
/E (     Sprint 1 covers real identity, scoped team context, milestone creation/read, one first submission per milestone and version-specific supervisor feedback. Sprint 2 adds team/planning management, revisions/history and team progress. Sprint 3 adds supervisor summary/filter/drill-down and completes hardening/verification. All continue the same application, repository and persistent history.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
360 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 270 0 R
/E (Work is submitted as a URL; the backend validates its syntax and never fetches it. The sender must check sharing permissions. There is no file upload, grading/approval workflow, chat, email notification, self-registration, password recovery, multi-course platform, public team directory, hard deletion of academic history or optional dark mode. Seeded accounts/team assignments are sufficient for S1; team-management behavior is still required in S2.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
