/Pg 27 0 R
/K [31]
>>
endobj
858 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 285 0 R
/E (Every HTTP interaction generates a unique UUID v4 tracking identifier returned in the X-Request-Id response header and recorded in the structured server log. Server errors are logged with method, route template, status code, duration, and correlation ID, while internal error stack traces and database credentials are completely redacted from public HTTP responses.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [32]
>>
endobj
859 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 286 0 R
/T (C.5 Concurrency, Locking, and State Transition Invariants)
/E (C.5 Concurrency, Locking, and State Transition Invariants)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
860 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 286 0 R
/T (C.5.1 Submission Pipeline & Deadline Serialization)
/E (C.5.1 Submission Pipeline & Deadline Serialization)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
861 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 286 0 R
/E (To eliminate race conditions between concurrent submissions and crossing deadline thresholds, SubmissionService.submit executes inside an atomic PostgreSQL transaction with two-phase row-level locks:)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
862 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3443 0 R
/E (Acquire Team Lock: SELECT id FROM teams WHERE id = $teamId FOR UPDATE Serializes cooperating application operations taking the same team lock; direct database writers must follow this protocol. The team lock does not automatically lock every related row.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
863 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3444 0 R
/E (Acquire Milestone Lock: SELECT id FROM milestones WHERE id = milestoneId AND team_id = teamId FOR UPDATE Locks the milestone row to prevent deadline adjustments during submission evaluation.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
864 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3445 0 R
/E (Scope Recheck and Rule Precedence: Recheck membership and milestone scope within the same transaction after locking.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
865 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3446 0 R
/E (Strict Precedence Invariant: The submission is evaluated against three non-negotiable gates in strict order:)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
866 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3447 0 R
/E (Gate 1 \(Cancellation\): If cancelled_at IS NOT NULL, reject immediately with 409 MILESTONE_CANCELLED.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
867 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3448 0 R
/E (Gate 2 \(Duplicate Submission\): Check if version 1 already exists. If present, reject immediately with 409 ALREADY_SUBMITTED.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
868 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3449 0 R
/E (Gate 3 \(Deadline Expiry\): After cancellation/duplicate checks, read date_trunc\('milliseconds', clock_timestamp\(\)\) once and compare it with the deadline. Persist that exact accepted value as submittedAt: acceptedAt > dueAt -> reject DEADLINE_PASSED; equality is accepted. Boundary equality \(acceptedAt = dueAt\) is accepted. If crossed \(acceptedAt > dueAt\), no row is written, and draft content is preserved on the client.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
869 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 286 0 R
/T (C.5.2 Feedback Mutation Idempotency & Retry Safety)
/E (C.5.2 Feedback Mutation Idempotency & Retry Safety)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
870 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 286 0 R
/E (Network failures between client and server risk duplicated supervisor feedback if the supervisor clicks "Submit" repeatedly. FeedbackService.createFeedback enforces idempotent retry safety:)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
871 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3450 0 R
/E (Tenant Scope Verification: Before checking the idempotency table, the service verifies that the supervisor owns the team corresponding to the submission. This prevents cross-tenant probing of clientRequestId UUIDs.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
872 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3451 0 R
/E (Deterministic Replay vs. Conflict Detection:)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
873 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3452 0 R
/E (If a feedback record with \(supervisor_id, client_request_id\) already exists:)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
874 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3453 0 R
/E (If the existing record's content and submission_id match the incoming request, the server returns HTTP 200 OK with the existing FeedbackDto \(deterministic replay\).)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
875 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3454 0 R
/E (If the clientRequestId matches but the content differs, the server rejects the request with HTTP 409 Conflict \(code: REQUEST_KEY_REUSED\), preventing accidental corruption.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
876 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3455 0 R
/E (Classified Rollback Retry: Writes use one transaction: scope lookup -> team row lock -> assignment/submission scope recheck -> supervisor/key lookup -> replay/conflict/insert. Only the actual feedback UUID unique constraint \(including its pinned PostgreSQL adapter shape\) or confirmed rolled-back contention may restart the whole scoped transaction, at most three attempts. Unknown outcomes/timeouts remain safe 503; arbitrary P2002 errors are not blindly retried. Reads scope and list in one repeatable-read transaction.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
877 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3456 0 R
/E (Immutable Client Recovery: The client freezes a UUID/body/exact-target intent after an unknown POST outcome and GETs saved feedback. A matching row confirms success. A successful GET without it permits a manual same-body/key retry; failed recovery keeps Save blocked. There is no automatic POST retry or Idempotency-Key header.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
