1002 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 292 0 R
/E (All routes below are under /api. Requests derive user/role from the DB-backed session, never a body/header identity. Domain writes run session -> required role -> source/CSRF -> JSON type/parser -> strict input -> scope/transaction/rule-> write. Login has its separate source/bootstrap guard; logout checks source and requires CSRF only for a valid session. Reads require a session and scope. Foreign/missing records share a generic 404; invalid identifiers may return 400 first. Student writes prohibited by role return 403 before resource scope is disclosed. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1003 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 292 0 R
/E (Successful JSON responses use {data}. Team, milestone, submission and feedback GETs add meta: {serverTime}; login/me return {data:{user,csrfToken}}. Logout is 204 with no body. Errors use {error:{code,message,fields}}; fields is a field-message object, possibly empty. X-Request-Id is a response header, not a request identity or body authority. Auth/private responses are Cache-Control: no-store.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1004 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 292 0 R
/E (Generated entity IDs are UUIDs. Generic team/resource checks and feedback UUID validation do not all enforce UUID v4; feedback payload validators accept RFC UUID versions 1-5 with valid variant bits and normalize to lowercase. The browser generates v4 request keys. Do not claim a stricter validator than the code implements. Response timestamps are UTC ISO strings with millisecond precision; UI displays Asia/Bangkok including seconds.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
